# Isolated publication requests

The helper is a one-request external Node process, not an extension-host API.
Its bounded stdin envelope carries a complete source snapshot. Only publication
commands are admitted; the shared runner owns diagnostics and transactions.


## Validate before loading the runner

The command must be first, and JSON mode is mandatory. Runtime validation belongs
here, not in ordinary CLI commands. No readiness chatter is sent on stdout.

```typescript: <<publication helper contract>>=
import type { SourceDocument } from './engine';
import type { Readable } from 'node:stream';

export const maximumRequestBytes = 32 * 1024 * 1024;
export interface PublicationRequest {
    args: string[];
    documents: SourceDocument[];
    publicationDocuments?: Record<string, SourceDocument[]>;
}

export function validateRuntime(versions: { node: string; electron?: string } = process.versions): void {
    const [major, minor] = versions.node.split('.').map(Number);
    if (versions.electron !== undefined || !Number.isInteger(major) || !Number.isInteger(minor)
        || major < 22 || (major === 22 && minor < 12)) {
        throw new Error('Publication helper requires external Node >=22.12 (not Electron)');
    }
}

export function parseRequest(text: string): PublicationRequest {
    const value: unknown = JSON.parse(text);
    if (!value || typeof value !== 'object' || Array.isArray(value)) {
        throw new Error('Expected a publication request object');
    }
    const request = value as Record<string, unknown>;
    const publicationDocuments = request.publicationDocuments;
    if (Object.keys(request).some(key => !['args', 'documents', 'publicationDocuments'].includes(key))
        || !Array.isArray(request.args) || !request.args.every(arg => typeof arg === 'string')
        || !['latex', 'pdf'].includes(request.args[0]) || !request.args.includes('--json')
        || request.args.some(arg => ['--help', '-h'].includes(arg))
        || !Array.isArray(request.documents)
        || publicationDocuments !== undefined && (!publicationDocuments || typeof publicationDocuments !== 'object'
            || Array.isArray(publicationDocuments)
            || Object.values(publicationDocuments).some(value => !Array.isArray(value)))) {
        throw new Error('Expected {args, documents}: latex or pdf first, --json required, no help');
    }
    return request as unknown as PublicationRequest;
}
```

## Bound request delivery

EOF terminates the single JSON envelope. Byte and time limits apply while reading,
not after an unbounded allocation. Cancellation rejects an incomplete request.

```typescript: <<publication helper input>>=
export function readRequest(input: Readable, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<string> {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        const chunks: Buffer[] = [];
        let bytes = 0;
        const cleanup = (): void => {
            clearTimeout(timer);
            input.removeListener('data', data);
            input.removeListener('end', end);
            input.removeListener('error', failed);
            signal.removeEventListener('abort', aborted);
            input.pause();
        };
        const failed = (error: Error): void => { cleanup(); reject(error); };
        const aborted = (): void => failed(new Error('Publication request cancelled'));
        const data = (chunk: Buffer | string): void => {
            const buffer = Buffer.isBuffer(chunk) ? chunk : Buffer.from(chunk);
            bytes += buffer.length;
            if (bytes > maximumRequestBytes) { failed(new Error('Publication request exceeds 32 MiB')); }
            else { chunks.push(buffer); }
        };
        const end = (): void => { cleanup(); resolve(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8')); };
        const timer = setTimeout(() => failed(new Error('Publication request timed out after 30000 ms')), 30000);
        signal.addEventListener('abort', aborted, { once: true });
        input.on('data', data).once('end', end).once('error', failed);
        if (signal.aborted) { aborted(); }
    });
}
```

## Keep cancellation latched across handoff

Listeners are installed before stdin is consumed and remain until the runner
settles. The final latch check and the runner's synchronous listener installation
have no asynchronous gap. Active Pandoc, diagram and PDF adapters handle their
own children; the runner prevents publication after cancellation. A signal before
JavaScript starts uses Node's default nonzero termination and cannot write files.

```typescript: <<publication helper lifecycle>>=
export async function publicationHelper(): Promise<number> {
    const controller = new AbortController();
    const signals = ['SIGINT', 'SIGTERM', 'SIGHUP'] as const;
    const cancel = (): void => { controller.abort(); };
    for (const signal of signals) { process.on(signal, cancel); }
    let output = '';
    try {
        validateRuntime();
        const request = parseRequest(await readRequest(process.stdin, controller.signal));
        const { run } = await import('./cli');
        if (controller.signal.aborted) { throw new Error('Publication request cancelled'); }
        const code = await run(request.args, {
            stdout: text => { output += text; },
            stderr: () => { throw new Error('Unexpected non-JSON publication output'); }
        }, undefined, undefined, undefined, undefined,
            { documents: request.documents, publicationDocuments: request.publicationDocuments });
        process.stdout.write(output);
        return code;
    } catch (error) {
        process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ schemaVersion: 1, command: 'publication', ok: false,
            diagnostics: [], outputs: [], errors: [error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)] }) + '\n');
        return 1;
    } finally {
        for (const signal of signals) { process.removeListener(signal, cancel); }
        process.stdin.pause();
    }
}
```

Only this entry executes the helper. Importing the CLI library cannot recursively
start a second command when the helper is bundled as CommonJS.

```typescript: <<publication helper entry>>=
if (require.main === module) {
    void publicationHelper().then(code => { process.exitCode = code; });
}
```
